From step 2 (2026-09-03): IO::K8s::AutoGen maps an inline nested 'type: object' with 'properties' to an opaque { Str => 1 } hash by design -- only $ref'd definitions become classes (t/04, t/57 depend on it). CRD openAPIV3Schema inlines everything, so add_crd must generate a class (inline struct or named nested class per D6) for every nested object with properties, otherwise the D3 field options below the top level never apply. Also: a schema default of JSON true/false on a boolean must be normalized (AutoGen does so via _normalize_bool since e5017837).

Step-3 Task 2 review: re-running add_crd for the same group/version/Kind on one IO::K8s instance returns the cached AutoGen class even if the manifest changed (class cache is by name). Documented in IO::K8s::CRD/add_crd POD; a fresh instance regenerates. Step 6's ensure_crd should decide whether to bust the cache (e.g. a per-call namespace suffix + map override) -- noted on kubernetes-rest 24.

